{"path":"std/cmp/index.html","title":"Module cmp","description":"Utilities for comparing and ordering values.","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"main-content"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Module cmp"}]},{"type":"text","value":"1.0.0 · "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/src/core/lib.rs.html#286","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Utilities for comparing and ordering values."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This module contains various tools for comparing and ordering values. In summary:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/cmp/trait.PartialEq.html","title":"trait std::cmp::PartialEq","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"PartialEq<Rhs>"}]},{"type":"text","value":" overloads the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"=="},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"!="},{"type":"text","value":" operators. In cases where "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Rhs"},{"type":"text","value":" (the right hand side’s type) is "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Self"},{"type":"text","value":", this trait corresponds to a partial equivalence relation."}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/cmp/trait.Eq.html","title":"trait std::cmp::Eq","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Eq"}]},{"type":"text","value":" indicates that the overloaded "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"=="},{"type":"text","value":" operator corresponds to an equivalence relation."}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/cmp/trait.Ord.html","title":"trait std::cmp::Ord","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Ord"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/cmp/trait.PartialOrd.html","title":"trait std::cmp::PartialOrd","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"PartialOrd"}]},{"type":"text","value":" are traits that allow you to define total and partial orderings between values, respectively. Implementing them overloads the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"<"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"<="},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":">"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":">="},{"type":"text","value":" operators."}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/cmp/enum.Ordering.html","title":"enum std::cmp::Ordering","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Ordering"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is an enum returned by the main functions of "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/cmp/trait.Ord.html","title":"trait std::cmp::Ord","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Ord"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/cmp/trait.PartialOrd.html","title":"trait std::cmp::PartialOrd","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"PartialOrd"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and describes an ordering of two values (less, equal, or greater)."}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/cmp/struct.Reverse.html","title":"struct std::cmp::Reverse","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Reverse"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is a struct that allows you to easily reverse an ordering."}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/cmp/trait.Ord.html#method.max","title":"method std::cmp::Ord::max","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"max"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/cmp/trait.Ord.html#method.min","title":"method std::cmp::Ord::min","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"min"}]},{"type":"text","value":" are functions that build off of "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/cmp/trait.Ord.html","title":"trait std::cmp::Ord","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Ord"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and allow you to find the maximum or minimum of two values."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For more details, see the respective documentation of each item in the list."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"structs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structs"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/cmp/struct.Reverse.html","title":"struct std::cmp::Reverse","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reverse"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"A helper struct for reverse ordering."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"enums","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enums"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/cmp/enum.Ordering.html","title":"enum std::cmp::Ordering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ordering"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"An "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Ordering"},{"type":"text","value":" is the result of a comparison between two values."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"traits","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Traits"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/cmp/trait.Eq.html","title":"trait std::cmp::Eq","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Eq"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Trait for comparisons corresponding to "},{"type":"link","href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equivalence_relation","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"equivalence relations"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/cmp/trait.Ord.html","title":"trait std::cmp::Ord","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ord"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Trait for types that form a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Total_order","title":